<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<tt xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml" xmlns:ttp="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#parameter" xmlns:tts="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#styling" ttp:timeBase="media" xml:lang="en">
  <head>
    <styling>
      <style xml:id="normal" tts:color="white" tts:fontFamily="sansSerif" tts:fontSize="100%" />
    </styling>
    <layout>
      <region xml:id="bottom" tts:displayAlign="after" tts:extent="100% 15%" tts:origin="0% 85%" tts:writingMode="lrtb" />
    </layout>
  </head>
  <body tts:color="white" region="bottom" style="normal">
    <div>
      <p begin="00:00:07.220" end="00:00:09.080" region="bottom">When you start a new software</p>
      <p begin="00:00:09.080" end="00:00:10.800" region="bottom">project, you're super excited</p>
      <p begin="00:00:10.800" end="00:00:12.900" region="bottom">about the potential of the</p>
      <p begin="00:00:12.900" end="00:00:14.140" region="bottom">project and you want to get</p>
      <p begin="00:00:14.140" end="00:00:16.220" region="bottom">moving as soon as possible,</p>
      <p begin="00:00:17.000" end="00:00:19.360" region="bottom">which is great. Often when</p>
      <p begin="00:00:19.360" end="00:00:21.720" region="bottom">that project matures and you</p>
      <p begin="00:00:21.720" end="00:00:23.060" region="bottom">get more customers and you get</p>
      <p begin="00:00:23.060" end="00:00:25.120" region="bottom">more users, things need to</p>
      <p begin="00:00:25.120" end="00:00:26.240" region="bottom">change because you start</p>
      <p begin="00:00:26.240" end="00:00:27.940" region="bottom">getting feedback from your</p>
      <p begin="00:00:27.940" end="00:00:29.160" region="bottom">customers. That's one thing.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:29.510" end="00:00:30.860" region="bottom">The other thing that happens</p>
      <p begin="00:00:30.860" end="00:00:33.080" region="bottom">is technologies change.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:33.420" end="00:00:34.740" region="bottom">Database systems might change.</p>
    </div>
  </body>
</tt>